---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Code from "../../components/docs/Code.astro";
import Callout from "../../components/docs/Callout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Quickstart" lead="Run Offhook on your machine, talk to an agent in your browser, then place a real phone call." slug="quickstart">
        <h2 id="requirements">What you need</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Python 3.13 and <a href="https://docs.astral.sh/uv/">uv</a>.</li>
          <li>Docker, to run Postgres.</li>
          <li>API keys from <a href="https://deepgram.com">Deepgram</a>, <a href="https://cartesia.ai">Cartesia</a> and <a href="https://console.groq.com">Groq</a>. All three have free tiers.</li>
          <li>For phone calls only: a <a href="https://www.plivo.com">Plivo</a> account with a number, and a way to expose your machine to the internet, such as <a href="https://ngrok.com">ngrok</a>.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="install">1. Install and configure</h2>
        <Code tabs={[{ label: "Terminal", lang: "bash", code: `git clone https://github.com/welldunai/offhook.git
cd offhook
uv venv && source .venv/bin/activate
uv pip install -e .
cp .env.example .env` }]} />
        <p>
          In <code>.env</code>, set <code>DEEPGRAM_API_KEY</code>, <code>CARTESIA_API_KEY</code>,
          <code>GROQ_API_KEY</code> and a master encryption key, which you can generate with:
        </p>
        <Code tabs={[{ label: "Terminal", lang: "bash", code: `python -c "import os,base64;print(base64.b64encode(os.urandom(32)).decode())"
# paste the output into .env as MASTER_ENCRYPTION_KEY` }]} />

        <h2 id="tenant">2. Start Postgres and create a dev tenant</h2>
        <Code tabs={[{ label: "Terminal", lang: "bash", code: `docker compose up -d
alembic upgrade head
python -m app.admin seed-dev --voice-id 05a69c2d-457a-4802-8f91-628cb158b522` }]} />
        <p>
          <code>seed-dev</code> creates a tenant, stores the provider keys from <code>.env</code>
          as encrypted <a href="/docs/connections/">connections</a>, creates a demo
          <a href="/docs/agents/">agent</a>, and prints two values:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>An <strong>API key</strong>, shown once. Export it so the examples below work as written: <code>export OFFHOOK_KEY="vk_dev_…"</code></li>
          <li>A <strong>DEV_AGENT_ID</strong>. Add it to <code>.env</code>.</li>
        </ul>
        <Callout kind="note">
          <code>seed-dev</code> is for local development only. On a real deployment, create
          the first tenant with <code>create-tenant</code> and add connections through the API.
          See <a href="/docs/deploying/">Deploying</a>.
        </Callout>

        <h2 id="browser">3. Talk to the agent in your browser</h2>
        <Code tabs={[{ label: "Terminal", lang: "bash", code: `python run.py` }]} />
        <p>
          Open <code>http://localhost:8000</code>, allow the microphone and start talking.
          The playground runs the same pipeline as a phone call over WebRTC, and shows live
          transcripts and the latency of each stage.
        </p>

        <h2 id="phone">4. Place a phone call</h2>
        <p>Phone calls need three more things:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Carrier keys.</strong> Add <code>PLIVO_AUTH_ID</code>, <code>PLIVO_AUTH_TOKEN</code> and <code>PLIVO_FROM_NUMBER</code> to <code>.env</code> before running <code>seed-dev</code>, so the demo agent gets a telephony connection. For Twilio, add a telephony connection through the API instead.</li>
          <li><strong>A public URL.</strong> The carrier calls back into Offhook when the call is answered. Run <code>ngrok http 8000</code> and set <code>PUBLIC_BASE_URL</code> in <code>.env</code> to the https address it prints.</li>
          <li><strong>The worker.</strong> It dials queued calls and delivers webhooks. Run <code>python -m app.worker</code> in a second terminal.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Restart <code>python run.py</code> so it picks up the new <code>.env</code>, then place the call:</p>
        <Code tabs={[{ label: "cURL", lang: "bash", code: `curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/v1/calls \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $OFFHOOK_KEY" \\
  -H "Idempotency-Key: first-call" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{
    "agent_id": "<DEV_AGENT_ID>",
    "to_number": "+14155550123",
    "context": { "patient_name": "Priya", "appointment_time": "Tuesday at 3 PM" }
  }'` }, { label: "Response", lang: "json", code: `{
  "id": "8f2c4d1e-6b7a-4c2e-9f1d-3a5b7c9e1f20",
  "status": "queued",
  "direction": "outbound",
  "provider_call_id": null
}` }]} />
        <Callout kind="note">
          Everything in <code>context</code> is added to the agent's prompt, so the agent
          knows those facts during the call.
        </Callout>

        <h2 id="result">5. Get the result</h2>
        <p>
          Fetch the call, or subscribe to <a href="/docs/webhooks/">webhooks</a> to be told
          when it changes. Once the call ends, it has an outcome, a transcript and a full
          event log.
        </p>
        <Code tabs={[{ label: "cURL", lang: "bash", code: `curl http://localhost:8000/v1/calls/8f2c4d1e-6b7a-4c2e-9f1d-3a5b7c9e1f20 \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $OFFHOOK_KEY"` }, { label: "Response", lang: "json", code: `{
  "id": "8f2c4d1e-6b7a-4c2e-9f1d-3a5b7c9e1f20",
  "status": "completed",
  "direction": "outbound",
  "to_number": "+14155550123",
  "from_number": "+14155550100",
  "provider_call_id": "abc-123",
  "outcome": { "summary": "Confirmed for Tuesday at 3 PM" },
  "error": null,
  "error_code": null,
  "has_recording": true,
  "tags": {},
  "created_at": "2026-10-15T10:00:00Z",
  "started_at": "2026-10-15T10:00:04Z",
  "ended_at": "2026-10-15T10:00:42Z"
}` }]} />

        <h2 id="next">Next steps</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/docs/connections/">Connections</a> and <a href="/docs/agents/">Agents</a>: set up your own agent instead of the demo one.</li>
          <li><a href="/docs/calls/">Calls</a>: everything you can read about a call.</li>
          <li><a href="/docs/self-hosting/">Self-hosting</a>: run Offhook in production.</li>
        </ul>

</DocsLayout>
